<title>NETHERLANDS: TABLE-ABN AMRO's LaSalle H1 net up 21 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-ABN AMRO's LaSalle H1 net up 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net income			   119.5  vs  98.8</p>
<p>Net income available to common 106.0  vs  84.3</p>
<p>    Net interest income		348.4  vs 269.1</p>
<p>    Non interest income		 98.6  vs 137.2</p>
<p>    Loss provision			46.8  vs  27.5</p>
<p>    Net chargeoffs			15.8  vs  18.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Chicago-based LaSalle National Corporation is a fully-owned U.S. unit of ABN AMRO Bank NV of the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Second quarter to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net income			    64.2  vs  50.8</p>
<p>Net income available to common  57.5  vs  43.6</p>
<p>    Net interest income		177.0  vs 137.5</p>
<p>    Non interest income		 47.7  vs  69.3</p>
<p>    Loss provision			24.5  vs  14.8</p>
<p>    Net chargeoffs			 9.4  vs  11.1</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
